{"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedHypergraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/Se","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/SE","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/SQ","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/SH","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"fileName":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift#L25"},"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule08OrientedaB0V","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","modules":[{"name":"IncidenceMatrixModule"}],"role":"symbol"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is the matrix of Gallo, Longo, Pallottino and Nguyen (1993). A directed graph’s edge is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"column with one source and one target, which gives the oriented incidence matrix of spectral","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graph theory (B·Bᵀ = L). The matrix conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedHypergraph"},{"text":", so the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithms (B- and F-connection, components, the clique expansion) run on it unchanged. It is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Two bit planes","anchor":"Two-bit-planes","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The sources and the targets are each stored as an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"text":", so a vertex can be on both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sides of a column. Its entry is then target − source = 0, with both bits kept.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sources(ofHyperedgeAt:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"targets(ofHyperedgeAt:)"},{"text":", the stars and equality read the planes,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so nothing is lost. A directed self-loop is such a column. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reversed"},{"text":" swaps the planes, negating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every entry, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transposed()"},{"text":" transposes each plane to give the dual. Both are O(1).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storage is 4·n·m\/8 bytes, so the matrix suits dense or small incidence. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":" is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sparse representation. Equality compares both planes cell for cell, with equal shape, so column"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order counts."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"sw